{"id":203901247025872,"type":"artist","name":"Joe Henry","artist":null,"year":1960,"weight":13,"info":{"tags":["singer-songwriter","folk","jazz","rock","alternative"],"country":"US","begin":"1960-12-02","kind":"Person","similar":["John Wesley Harding","Peter Case","Michael Penn","Patty Griffin","Robyn Hitchcock","Robbie Fulks","Tift Merritt","John Hiatt","Greg Brown","Jeffrey Foucault"],"disambiguation":"US singer-songwriter, guitarist & producer","img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Joe-Henry_DSC00919.jpg?width=500","bio":"Nacido en 1960 en Carolina del Norte, Joe Henry es uno de los músicos-escritores de canciones más relevantes de esa fórmula musical bautizada como “americana”. “Su sonido se puede definir como una mezcla equilibrada y vibrante de gran complejidad rítmica, donde sobresalen las tonalidades oscuras y enigmáticas”, explica Javier Díaz. Henry experimenta con texturas sónicas –guitarras con ecos, “delays”, sintetizadores- y toma elementos del jazz, el soul, el blues, el country-rock y el pop."},"works":[{"id":69586504237722,"type":"album","name":"Shuffletown","artist":"Joe Henry","year":1990,"weight":14,"yt":"LMp4jQRjmIY","src":"books,charts,musthear","from":{"books":[{"name":"Scaruffi","title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000 (Piero Scaruffi)"}],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":13018320481353,"name":"Scaruffi 1990s","rank":807,"scaruffi":7.0}],"n_lists":1}},{"id":207049630038378,"type":"album","name":"Short Man's Room","artist":"Joe Henry","year":1992,"weight":11,"yt":"ityCr9AVFqY","src":"books,musthear","from":{"books":[{"name":"Scaruffi","title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000 (Piero Scaruffi)"}],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":103254340346721,"name":"RYM Top — Regional Music — Americana","rank":122,"scaruffi":null},{"id":118798969175346,"name":"RYM Top — Country — Alt-Country","rank":132,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":2}},{"id":233152012913929,"type":"album","name":"Kindness Of The World","artist":"Joe Henry","year":1993,"weight":6