ie Lucky (1993). New York's Joe Henry (3), staged one of the most impressive metamorphosis, the epitome of his generation's stylistic wandering. On his third album, the acoustic Shuffletown (1990), featuring guitarist T-Bone Burnett and jazz musicians Don Cherry (trumpet), Cecil McBee (bass) and Phil Kelly (piano), Henry embraced Van Morrison's folk-jazz, while Short Man's Room (1992) echoed the Band's gospel-rock and Bob Dylan's folk-rock, and Kindness Of The World…"}],"podcast":[],"awards":[],"concerts":[],"xref":[],"charts":[{"id":69586504237722,"type":"album","name":"Shuffletown","work_year":1990,"list_id":13018320481353,"list":"Scaruffi 1990s","src":"charts","rank":807,"year":1990,"note":null,"yt":"LMp4jQRjmIY","scaruffi":7.0},{"id":207049630038378,"type":"album","name":"Short Man's Room","list_id":118798969175346,"list":"RYM Top — Country — Alt-Country","src":"musthear","rank":132,"year":1992,"note":null,"yt":"ityCr9AVFqY","scaruffi":null},{"id":207049630038378,"type":"album","name":"Short Man's Room","list_id":103254340346721,"list":"RYM Top — Regional Music — Americana","src":"musthear","rank":122,"year":1992,"note":null,"yt":"ityCr9AVFqY","scaruffi":null},{"id":95832438104475,"type":"album","name":"Trampoline","list_id":103254340346721,"list":"RYM Top — Regional Music — Americana","src":"musthear","rank":162,"year":1996,"note":null,"yt":"w2mgzIS1nPo","scaruffi":7.0},{"id":95832438104475,"type":"album","name":"Trampoline","work_year":1996,"list_id":13018320481353,"list":"Scaruffi 1990s","src":"charts","rank":808,"year":1996,"note":null,"yt":"w2mgzIS1nPo","scaruffi":7.0},{"id":235608951104087,"type":"album","name":"Scar","list_id":103254340346721,"list":"RYM Top — Regional Music — Americana","src":"musthear","rank":73,"year":2001,"note":null,"yt":"5OW8xMDzdrE","scaruffi":null}],"lists":[]}